      _push(`<div class="status-badge" data-v-911a4756><span data-v-911a4756>Live</span></div><img${ssrRenderAttr("src", _imports_0)} alt="The home page of The NeO Frequency, with its headline over Floris&#39;s ocean film and buttons for SID™ and the two-minute Signal Check" class="hero-shot" data-v-911a4756><h1 data-v-911a4756>The NeO Frequency</h1><p class="tagline" data-v-911a4756>Organisational Coherence Practice, Floris Robert Slob</p><div class="hero-meta" data-v-911a4756><span class="meta-tag" data-v-911a4756>Role: Designer, Developer &amp; Wix Migration</span><span class="meta-tag" data-v-911a4756>Advisory Practice &amp; Thought Leadership</span><a href="https://www.theneofrequency.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="meta-tag link-tag" data-v-911a4756>theneofrequency.com →</a></div><div class="fee-banner" data-v-911a4756><span class="fee-banner-label" data-v-911a4756>No Development Fee</span><p data-v-911a4756>Redesigned, rebuilt and moved off Wix with no development fee. The practice is on our monthly hosting, maintenance and support plan.</p></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-911a4756><div class="detail-container" data-v-911a4756><h2 data-v-911a4756>Overview</h2><p data-v-911a4756> Floris Robert Slob is a transformation and change leader with more than 25 years of global business transformation behind him. Through The NeO Frequency, from the Geneva region of Switzerland, he shows organisations where their intent weakens, diverges or gets blocked on the way to results, and his Signal Integrity Diagnostic™ (SID™) measures it. We rebuilt his website from the ground up: one that holds together on every screen, brings his diagnostic onto the site itself, and gives his writing a proper home. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-911a4756><div class="detail-container" data-v-911a4756><h2 data-v-911a4756>The Challenge</h2><p data-v-911a4756> The ideas were sharp, but the website was letting them down. It was built on Wix with fixed layouts, so on common laptop screens the buttons at the right edge were cut off, and on tablets the desktop layout ran off the side of the screen, taking headlines and navigation with it. The Signal Check, the easiest way in for a prospective client, sent visitors away to a generic Google Form, and twelve essays sat in a default blog feed that made them hard to browse. For a practice about signals that get lost between intent and results, the website was losing its own. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-911a4756><div class="detail-container" data-v-911a4756><h2 data-v-911a4756>Two Days to a Prototype</h2><div class="highlight-box" data-v-911a4756><span class="highlight-number" data-v-911a4756>2 days</span><span class="highlight-label" data-v-911a4756>from offering a better version to a working prototype he could click through</span></div><p data-v-911a4756> Floris had not asked for a new website. I had been following his posts on LinkedIn and asking about his ideas when I noticed his site breaking on my laptop. I offered to show him a better version, with no obligation, and about two days later he could click through it. That is how every project with us starts: you react to something real, then decide. In his words: &quot;At first I thought my old website was still OK, but after he showed me what it could look like, I was sold!&quot; </p></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-911a4756><div class="detail-container" data-v-911a4756><h2 data-v-911a4756>Inside the New Site</h2><div class="screens-grid" data-v-911a4756><figure class="screen screen--wide" data-v-911a4756><img${ssrRenderAttr("src", _imports_1)} alt="The Field&#39;s article browser, with filters for theme and content type above three article cards" loading="lazy" data-v-911a4756><figcaption data-v-911a4756>The Field: his essays, filtered by theme and type, each with a key takeaway and related reading.</figcaption></figure><figure class="screen" data-v-911a4756><img${ssrRenderAttr("src", _imports_2)} alt="The first Signal Check question, on shared priorities, answered on a scale of 1 to 5" loading="lazy" data-v-911a4756><figcaption data-v-911a4756>The Signal Check, now on his own site: six questions, answered from where the visitor sits.</figcaption></figure><figure class="screen" data-v-911a4756><img${ssrRenderAttr("src", _imports_3)} alt="A Signal Check result reading Mixed signals, with a score of 16 out of 25 and the visitor&#39;s story below it" loading="lazy" data-v-911a4756><figcaption data-v-911a4756>An instant result, shaped to the visitor&#39;s role and scored in the browser. A copy goes by email only on request.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-911a4756><div class="detail-container" data-v-911a4756><h2 data-v-911a4756>What I Built</h2><p class="section-intro" data-v-911a4756> A practice site built to his own specification, with his diagnostic, his services and his writing in one place. </p><div class="features-grid" data-v-911a4756><div class="feature-card" data-v-911a4756><div class="feature-icon" data-v-911a4756>🧭</div><h3 data-v-911a4756>The Signal Check</h3><p data-v-911a4756> His two-minute diagnostic, brought onto the site in place of a Google Form: a role, six questions and an instant result, with a copy by email on request. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-911a4756><div class="feature-icon" data-v-911a4756>📡</div><h3 data-v-911a4756>SID™, the Flagship</h3><p data-v-911a4756> A page for the Signal Integrity Diagnostic™, with its five-stage Translation Journey, what clients receive, his own film and the brochure to download. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-911a4756><div class="feature-icon" data-v-911a4756>🌿</div><h3 data-v-911a4756>The Field</h3><p data-v-911a4756> A home for his writing: twelve essays moved over from Wix and room for every new one, filtered by theme and type, with takeaways and related reading. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-911a4756><div class="feature-icon" data-v-911a4756>💡</div><h3 data-v-911a4756>Three Concept Pages</h3><p data-v-911a4756> Organisational Coherence, Signal Integrity and Human Capacity, each explained on a page of its own, so every idea can be linked and found. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-911a4756><div class="feature-icon" data-v-911a4756>✉️</div><h3 data-v-911a4756>The Field Letter</h3><p data-v-911a4756> A newsletter sign-up with an automatic welcome email, and a template he uses to write and send each issue himself. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-911a4756><div class="feature-icon" data-v-911a4756>🤝</div><h3 data-v-911a4756>Four Ways to Work Together</h3><p data-v-911a4756> Diagnose, Navigate, Realign and Reframe: SID™, Executive Advisory, Alignment Workshops, and Keynotes &amp; Signature Sessions, each with its own page. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-911a4756><div class="feature-icon" data-v-911a4756>💬</div><h3 data-v-911a4756>Testimonials &amp; About</h3><p data-v-911a4756> Six client accounts carried over with every word kept, and an About page on the path that led him to this work. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-911a4756><div class="feature-icon" data-v-911a4756>📅</div><h3 data-v-911a4756>Connect Page</h3><p data-v-911a4756> An enquiry form that lands in his inbox, a link to book a call, and his direct details for anyone who would rather write. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-911a4756><div class="feature-icon" data-v-911a4756>🔀</div><h3 data-v-911a4756>Nothing Lost in the Move</h3><p data-v-911a4756> Old Wix addresses, blog posts included, now lead to their new pages, so links people already shared keep working. </p></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-911a4756><div class="detail-container" data-v-911a4756><h2 data-v-911a4756>Even the Holding Page Had a Job</h2><p data-v-911a4756> Before launch, Floris asked for a simple notice on his domain, so visitors would learn that a new site was on the way instead of landing on the old one. A line of text would have done that. Instead, the holding page previewed the new home page, with his ocean film and the announcement he approved, a way to start a conversation, and the SID™ brochure to download. It stood in for the old site at his own address until the new one launched in the first half of November 2026, as the page promised. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-911a4756><div class="detail-container" data-v-911a4756><h2 data-v-911a4756>Tech Stack &amp; Hosting</h2><div class="tech-grid" data-v-911a4756><div class="tech-card" data-v-911a4756><h3 data-v-911a4756>Astro</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-911a4756>Framework</span><p data-v-911a4756> Every page prerendered to static HTML, with server code only where it earns its place: the Signal Check&#39;s emailed result and the newsletter sign-up. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-911a4756><h3 data-v-911a4756>Tailwind CSS</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-911a4756>Design System</span><p data-v-911a4756> His brand colours defined once as tokens, with the teal and green drawn a shade deeper where needed, so text passes WCAG AA contrast. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-911a4756><h3 data-v-911a4756>Cloudflare</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-911a4756>Hosting &amp; DNS</span><p data-v-911a4756> Served from Cloudflare&#39;s edge, with his domain moved over from Wix and his ocean film re-encoded to under a quarter of its original size. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-911a4756><h3 data-v-911a4756>Resend</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-911a4756>Email</span><p data-v-911a4756> Signal Check results and The Field Letter, sent from his own verified domain, with the subscriber list kept in his own account. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-911a4756><h3 data-v-911a4756>Structured SEO</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-911a4756>Discoverability</span><p data-v-911a4756> Structured data that connects the practice, its founder, services, concepts and articles, plus social cards, a sitemap and RSS, so search engines and AI assistants read the site accurately. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-911a4756><h3 data-v-911a4756>Playwright</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-911a4756>Testing</span><p data-v-911a4756> Every page checked at ten screen widths, from 320px phones to 2560px monitors, along with the menus, the forms and the Signal Check itself. </p></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-911a4756><div class="detail-container" data-v-911a4756><h2 data-v-911a4756>What the Client Said</h2><div class="testimonial-card" data-v-911a4756><div class="testimonial-quote-mark" data-v-911a4756>&quot;</div><blockquote class="testimonial-text" data-v-911a4756> Where do I start? Quan, a person who showed up in my LinkedIn posts as somebody who was eager to understand what I was talking about related to the NeO Frequency. At some stage, he decided to tell me that my website didn&#39;t really show up as intended on his laptop and that there were issues with mobile phones as well. On top of that, he was also seeing some other aspects of my, in the meantime redundant website, that he could improve, and he was happy to show me how. He proposed a different design, one that reacts faster too and obviously would never have screen presentation issues anymore. About 2 days later, he came back to me with a design prototype. <br data-v-911a4756><br data-v-911a4756> I guess here I really need to warn you! <br data-v-911a4756><br data-v-911a4756> At first I thought my old website was still OK, but after he showed me what it could look like, I was sold! So be careful, people; make sure you are happy to let him do his magic, because the moment you agree with him WITHOUT ANY OBLIGATION and for Free (!), that he builds a prototype/design website for you, that&#39;s it! You will want that design coming to life! I promise you. <br data-v-911a4756><br data-v-911a4756> Quan is more than capable in everything that he does, and he goes way beyond the famous &quot;extra mile&quot;. To give you an example: When I asked him to provide me with a &quot;Work in progress&quot; page for my domain, so that people could no longer see my website, but were informed that a new website was under construction, his message became so much more elaborate, including a sneak preview of the new landing page, including direct ways to contact me or download a brochure (while waiting for my website to be live). <br data-v-911a4756><br data-v-911a4756> Quan can really perceive very quickly what it is you need, sometimes even before you do. During your website project, I&#39;m sure he will pleasantly surprise you over and over again. All the way to delivery day. And yes, sometimes, it even feels like he could read my mind too :-). Last but not least, I admire his &quot;skill-wanderer&quot; philosophy; he doesn&#39;t charge you anything for the website either. It&#39;s built completely for FREE. So what&#39;s the catch, you may think? Well, isn&#39;t that obvious? He IS the CATCH! <br data-v-911a4756><br data-v-911a4756> I would highly recommend Quan to anybody looking for a highly proactive, intelligent, smart, full-stack developer and AI integrator. Thank you so much, Quan, for your precious time and energy invested in our collaboration so far. The result is there for the world to see: https://theneofrequency.com. I truly wish our collaboration will bear bigger fruit in the near future for both of us! </blockquote><div class="testimonial-author" data-v-911a4756><img${ssrRenderAttr("src", _imports_4)} alt="Floris Robert Slob" class="testimonial-avatar" loading="lazy" data-v-911a4756><div class="testimonial-meta" data-v-911a4756><p class="testimonial-name" data-v-911a4756>Floris Robert Slob</p><p class="testimonial-role" data-v-911a4756>Senior Transformation &amp; Change Leader · Founder of The NeO Frequency</p><p class="testimonial-source" data-v-911a4756>Shared on LinkedIn, 10 November 2026</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-911a4756><div class="detail-container" data-v-911a4756><h2 data-v-911a4756>My Role</h2><p class="section-intro" data-v-911a4756> A prototype first, then his specification, then the move: </p><div class="role-list" data-v-911a4756><div class="role-item" data-v-911a4756>Noticed his site breaking on my laptop and built a working prototype of a better one, with no obligation.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-911a4756>Built the full site to his specification, then refined it through several rounds of his notes, down to the punctuation.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-911a4756>Brought his Signal Check onto the site, with results by email from his own domain.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-911a4756>Moved twelve essays and six testimonials off Wix with every word kept, and redirected the old addresses.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-911a4756>Set up email sending, the newsletter and its welcome email in his own accounts, and moved his domain to Cloudflare.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-911a4756>Built a holding page that previewed the new site until launch.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-911a4756>Tested every page at ten screen widths, so nothing is cut off on any screen again.</div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-911a4756><div class="detail-container" data-v-911a4756><h2 data-v-911a4756>Why There Was No Development Fee</h2><blockquote class="featured-quote" data-v-911a4756> Floris did not come looking for a new website, so the fair way to start was to show him one. The prototype came first, with no obligation, and he decided after seeing it. As with every accepted project, there was no development fee: a monthly fee covers hosting, maintenance and support instead, and like every client&#39;s fee, it helps fund free education. </blockquote></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-911a4756><div class="detail-container" data-v-911a4756><h2 data-v-911a4756>Project Status</h2><div class="status-box" data-v-911a4756><span class="status-indicator" data-v-911a4756>Live</span><p data-v-911a4756> The new site has been live at his own domain since November 2026. New essays go up as Floris writes them, he sends The Field Letter himself, and hosting, maintenance and support are covered by the monthly plan. </p></div></div></section><section class="cta-section" data-v-911a4756><div class="cta-container" data-v-911a4756><h2 data-v-911a4756>Know Your Field Better Than Your Website Shows?</h2><p data-v-911a4756> We help consultants and advisers turn deep expertise into a site that holds up on every screen. Tell us what you do, and you&#39;ll see a free working prototype before you commit to anything. </p><div class="cta-buttons" data-v-911a4756>`);
