      _push(`<div class="status-badge" data-v-16c2f3db><span data-v-16c2f3db>Live</span></div><img${ssrRenderAttr("src", _imports_0)} alt="Matt Harr Speaker" class="hero-visual" data-v-16c2f3db><h1 data-v-16c2f3db>Matt Harr Speaker</h1><p class="tagline" data-v-16c2f3db>Professional Speaking Website</p><div class="hero-meta" data-v-16c2f3db><span class="meta-tag" data-v-16c2f3db>Role: Designer, Developer &amp; Business Adviser</span><span class="meta-tag" data-v-16c2f3db>Personal Brand &amp; Speaking Business</span><a href="https://mattharrspeaker.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="meta-tag link-tag" data-v-16c2f3db>mattharrspeaker.com →</a></div><div class="fee-banner" data-v-16c2f3db><span class="fee-banner-label" data-v-16c2f3db>No Development Fee</span><p data-v-16c2f3db>Designed, built, and launched with no development fee. Matt is on our monthly hosting, maintenance and support plan.</p></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="detail-container" data-v-16c2f3db><h2 data-v-16c2f3db>Overview</h2><p data-v-16c2f3db> Matt Harr spent 35 years inside schools as a teacher, coach, and mentor. He is a 1989 San Francisco Giants draft pick, a five-time State Coach of the Year with over 400 career wins, and the author of <em data-v-16c2f3db>Back When Consequences Weren&#39;t Optional</em>. What he did not have was a professional home online where superintendents, principals, and athletic directors could understand his message and book him to speak. I designed and built that home, and stayed on as a sounding board while he shaped the speaking business around it. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="detail-container" data-v-16c2f3db><h2 data-v-16c2f3db>The Challenge</h2><p data-v-16c2f3db> Matt arrived with three decades of stories, not a brand. The raw material was extraordinary, but it was scattered across anecdotes, a book manuscript, and a lifetime of coaching notes. The work was to find the through-line, turn it into a positioning a school district would recognise in seconds, and then build a site around it that answers the questions a decision-maker actually asks: what does he speak about, how long is it, who has he worked with, and how do I get him on my calendar? </p></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="detail-container" data-v-16c2f3db><h2 data-v-16c2f3db>Finding the Message</h2><div class="highlight-box" data-v-16c2f3db><span class="highlight-number" data-v-16c2f3db>3 pillars</span><span class="highlight-label" data-v-16c2f3db>alignment, accountability, relationships</span></div><p data-v-16c2f3db> Everything on the site resolves to one promise: helping schools build cultures where accountability is expected, relationships are strong, and leadership develops naturally. That sentence did not exist when we started. It came out of the consulting conversations, and once we had it, every page, headline, and call-to-action had somewhere to point. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="detail-container" data-v-16c2f3db><h2 data-v-16c2f3db>What I Built</h2><p class="section-intro" data-v-16c2f3db> A nine-page speaking site built to turn an interested school leader into a booking enquiry. </p><div class="features-grid" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="feature-card" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="feature-icon" data-v-16c2f3db>🎤</div><h3 data-v-16c2f3db>Speaking Page</h3><p data-v-16c2f3db> Five clearly scoped offerings, from 45 to 75 minute culture keynotes to multi-day educator leadership workshops, student assemblies, and coach and athletic director clinics, each with its own format and audience. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="feature-icon" data-v-16c2f3db>📋</div><h3 data-v-16c2f3db>Programs Page</h3><p data-v-16c2f3db> The detail a superintendent needs before committing budget: what the session covers, who it is for, and what a school walks away with. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="feature-icon" data-v-16c2f3db>📖</div><h3 data-v-16c2f3db>About Page</h3><p data-v-16c2f3db> The credential stack told as a story rather than a résumé, with the coaching record and the classroom years doing the persuading. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="feature-icon" data-v-16c2f3db>💬</div><h3 data-v-16c2f3db>Testimonials Page</h3><p data-v-16c2f3db> Named endorsements with photographs from the superintendents and athletic directors who have already brought Matt into their buildings. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="feature-icon" data-v-16c2f3db>✍️</div><h3 data-v-16c2f3db>Writing Archive</h3><p data-v-16c2f3db> Over twenty long-form essays with an RSS feed, giving Matt a publishing habit that keeps the site earning search traffic between bookings. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="feature-icon" data-v-16c2f3db>📚</div><h3 data-v-16c2f3db>Book Page</h3><p data-v-16c2f3db> A dedicated page for <em data-v-16c2f3db>Back When Consequences Weren&#39;t Optional</em>, linked straight through to Amazon. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="feature-icon" data-v-16c2f3db>📨</div><h3 data-v-16c2f3db>Speaking Request Form</h3><p data-v-16c2f3db> A qualified enquiry form capturing event type, date, location, and organisation, so Matt receives a scopeable request rather than a blank message. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="feature-icon" data-v-16c2f3db>♿</div><h3 data-v-16c2f3db>Policy Pages</h3><p data-v-16c2f3db> Accessibility statement, privacy policy, and cookie policy, because a site selling to public school districts needs to hold up to procurement. </p></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="detail-container" data-v-16c2f3db><h2 data-v-16c2f3db>Tech Stack &amp; Hosting</h2><div class="tech-grid" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="tech-card" data-v-16c2f3db><h3 data-v-16c2f3db>Astro</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-16c2f3db>Framework</span><p data-v-16c2f3db> Static generation with almost no JavaScript shipped to the browser. Pages load instantly on a school district network, which is exactly where this site gets opened. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-16c2f3db><h3 data-v-16c2f3db>Cloudflare</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-16c2f3db>Hosting</span><p data-v-16c2f3db> Fast global delivery on a lightweight build, which keeps Matt&#39;s monthly care fee small. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-16c2f3db><h3 data-v-16c2f3db>Web3Forms</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-16c2f3db>Enquiry Handling</span><p data-v-16c2f3db> Speaking requests are delivered straight to Matt&#39;s inbox with no backend to maintain and no monthly form-service subscription. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-16c2f3db><h3 data-v-16c2f3db>Structured SEO &amp; RSS</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-16c2f3db>Discoverability</span><p data-v-16c2f3db> Canonical URLs, Open Graph cards, and an RSS feed on the writing archive, so every new essay compounds into search visibility. </p></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="detail-container" data-v-16c2f3db><h2 data-v-16c2f3db>What the Client Said</h2><div class="testimonial-card" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="testimonial-quote-mark" data-v-16c2f3db>&quot;</div><blockquote class="testimonial-text" data-v-16c2f3db> Quan did an outstanding job building my professional speaking website. He took my ideas, stories, and experience and turned them into a polished website that clearly represents who I am and the message I want to share. <br data-v-16c2f3db><br data-v-16c2f3db> What sets Quan apart, however, is that his help went far beyond designing a website. He has been a trusted business adviser throughout the process, offering honest feedback and practical guidance on how to position myself, present my services, reach potential clients, and grow my speaking business. He understands both the creative and business sides of building a professional brand. <br data-v-16c2f3db><br data-v-16c2f3db> Quan is knowledgeable, dependable, patient, and genuinely invested in the success of the people he works with. I highly recommend him to anyone looking for an excellent website and a trusted partner who will help them think strategically about their business. </blockquote><div class="testimonial-author" data-v-16c2f3db><img${ssrRenderAttr("src", _imports_1)} alt="Matt Harr" class="testimonial-avatar" loading="lazy" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="testimonial-meta" data-v-16c2f3db><p class="testimonial-name" data-v-16c2f3db>Matt Harr</p><p class="testimonial-role" data-v-16c2f3db>Speaker on school culture and leadership · Author of Back When Consequences Weren&#39;t Optional</p><p class="testimonial-source" data-v-16c2f3db>Shared on LinkedIn, 29 August 2026</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="detail-container" data-v-16c2f3db><h2 data-v-16c2f3db>My Role</h2><p class="section-intro" data-v-16c2f3db> This engagement was half build, half business advice: </p><div class="role-list" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="role-item" data-v-16c2f3db>Ran the positioning conversations that turned 35 years of stories into a single speaking promise.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-16c2f3db>Designed the visual identity, page architecture, and information hierarchy.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-16c2f3db>Developed and deployed the full site, from static build to domain and hosting setup.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-16c2f3db>Advised on service packaging, pricing posture, and how to present offerings to school districts.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-16c2f3db>Set up the writing archive and RSS feed so Matt could keep publishing without me.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-16c2f3db>Stayed available as a business sounding board as the speaking practice grew.</div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="detail-container" data-v-16c2f3db><h2 data-v-16c2f3db>Why There Was No Development Fee</h2><blockquote class="featured-quote" data-v-16c2f3db> There was no development fee because that is how we work with every accepted project. Instead of a big bill up front, Matt pays a small monthly fee for hosting, maintenance and support, which keeps me invested in his site long after launch. For someone who spent 35 years making sure the kids in his classrooms and on his teams had someone in their corner, a partner who stays felt like the right way to work. </blockquote></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="detail-container" data-v-16c2f3db><h2 data-v-16c2f3db>Project Status</h2><div class="status-box" data-v-16c2f3db><span class="status-indicator" data-v-16c2f3db>Live</span><p data-v-16c2f3db> The site is live and Matt publishes to it independently, while we look after hosting, maintenance and support under his monthly plan. Static generation means there is no server to patch and no database to back up, which keeps that monthly fee small. The architecture leaves room to add a booking calendar or a paid course if the speaking business calls for it. </p></div></div></section><section class="cta-section" data-v-16c2f3db><div class="cta-container" data-v-16c2f3db><h2 data-v-16c2f3db>Building Something You Need to Be Taken Seriously For?</h2><p data-v-16c2f3db> Whether you are launching a speaking practice, a studio, or a product, we build the site and think through the business with you. Tell us what you are working on. </p><div class="cta-buttons" data-v-16c2f3db>`);
