      _push(`<div class="status-badge" data-v-0a5fd39e><span data-v-0a5fd39e>Live</span></div><img${ssrRenderAttr("src", _imports_0)} alt="Broad Strokes Studio" class="hero-logo" data-v-0a5fd39e><h1 data-v-0a5fd39e>Broad Strokes Studio</h1><p class="tagline" data-v-0a5fd39e>Bespoke Calligraphy Studio, Tucson, Arizona</p><div class="hero-meta" data-v-0a5fd39e><span class="meta-tag" data-v-0a5fd39e>Role: Designer, Developer &amp; Commerce Setup</span><span class="meta-tag" data-v-0a5fd39e>Artisan Studio &amp; Commissions</span><a href="https://broadstrokesstudio.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="meta-tag link-tag" data-v-0a5fd39e>broadstrokesstudio.com →</a></div><div class="fee-banner" data-v-0a5fd39e><span class="fee-banner-label" data-v-0a5fd39e>No Development Fee</span><p data-v-0a5fd39e>Two months of design and development with no development fee. Jack is on our monthly hosting, maintenance and support plan.</p></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="detail-container" data-v-0a5fd39e><h2 data-v-0a5fd39e>Overview</h2><p data-v-0a5fd39e> Jack Passananti is a writer, calligrapher, and illuminator who hand-letters on archival paper: scripture, literary passages, family trees, wedding vows. Work like that sells on craft and trust, and neither survives a generic template. Over two months we built Broad Strokes a website that carries the same care as the pieces it sells, with a commission process, a priced catalogue, and checkout that lets a client commit without a back-and-forth email thread. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="detail-container" data-v-0a5fd39e><h2 data-v-0a5fd39e>The Challenge</h2><p data-v-0a5fd39e> Bespoke work is hard to sell online. Buyers cannot touch the paper, cannot feel the weight of the gilding, and have no reference point for what a hand-lettered 16x20 should cost. Most calligraphy sites solve this by hiding prices behind a contact form, which loses the buyer. The brief was to make the value legible: show the real work, explain the process honestly, and publish the prices so a serious client can self-qualify before the first conversation. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="detail-container" data-v-0a5fd39e><h2 data-v-0a5fd39e>A Constraint That Defined the Site: No AI Imagery</h2><img${ssrRenderAttr("src", _imports_1)} alt="Hand-lettered calligraphy in progress" class="inline-visual" data-v-0a5fd39e><p data-v-0a5fd39e> Jack was firm from the first consultation: every piece shown on the site has to be a photograph of real work, not a generated image. For a studio whose entire promise is that a human hand made this, that is not a preference, it is the product. It meant the build waited on photography, and it meant designing layouts around the pieces that actually existed rather than filling grids with stock. The constraint made the site slower to finish and considerably more honest. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="detail-container" data-v-0a5fd39e><h2 data-v-0a5fd39e>What I Built</h2><p class="section-intro" data-v-0a5fd39e> A seven-page studio site with a full commission funnel, from first look to paid deposit. </p><div class="features-grid" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="feature-card" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="feature-icon" data-v-0a5fd39e>🖋️</div><h3 data-v-0a5fd39e>Landing Page</h3><p data-v-0a5fd39e> A single promise, words of enduring beauty created to be cherished for generations, carried by one full-bleed photograph of the studio desk rather than a wall of copy. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="feature-icon" data-v-0a5fd39e>📜</div><h3 data-v-0a5fd39e>Commissions Page</h3><p data-v-0a5fd39e> Three clear categories: custom artwork, family heritage pieces, and special occasions, each with the kind of text the studio letters and the sizes available. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="feature-icon" data-v-0a5fd39e>💰</div><h3 data-v-0a5fd39e>Published Pricing</h3><p data-v-0a5fd39e> Eight priced options across four formats, framed and unframed, from an 8x10 at $225 to a 16x20 framed at $1,148. No quote request required to find out what a piece costs. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="feature-icon" data-v-0a5fd39e>🖼️</div><h3 data-v-0a5fd39e>Gallery</h3><p data-v-0a5fd39e> Photographed pieces, shot as real artefacts on real paper, giving buyers the texture and scale reference a product description cannot. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="feature-icon" data-v-0a5fd39e>🧭</div><h3 data-v-0a5fd39e>Process Page</h3><p data-v-0a5fd39e> The three phases spelled out: private consultation on intent and text, a composition study approved before lettering begins, then final artwork with optional gilding, diapering, rubrication, and framing. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="feature-icon" data-v-0a5fd39e>📅</div><h3 data-v-0a5fd39e>Consultation Booking</h3><p data-v-0a5fd39e> A 30-minute private consultation bookable directly through Cal.com, because a short call is the cleanest way to scope custom work. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="feature-icon" data-v-0a5fd39e>✉️</div><h3 data-v-0a5fd39e>Inquiry Page</h3><p data-v-0a5fd39e> For clients who want to describe a piece in writing before committing to a call. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="feature-icon" data-v-0a5fd39e>💳</div><h3 data-v-0a5fd39e>Stripe Checkout</h3><p data-v-0a5fd39e> Eight Stripe payment links, one per size and framing option, each tagged with a client reference so Jack knows exactly which piece was purchased without reconciling anything by hand. </p></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="detail-container" data-v-0a5fd39e><h2 data-v-0a5fd39e>Tech Stack &amp; Hosting</h2><div class="tech-grid" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="tech-card" data-v-0a5fd39e><h3 data-v-0a5fd39e>Astro</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-0a5fd39e>Framework</span><p data-v-0a5fd39e> Static generation, chosen so the large photographs of the work load fast and the pages stay crisp on a phone screen, which is where most people first see a piece. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-0a5fd39e><h3 data-v-0a5fd39e>Stripe Payment Links</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-0a5fd39e>Commerce</span><p data-v-0a5fd39e> Full checkout without running a store. No cart, no inventory system, no platform fee stacked on top of Stripe&#39;s own, and nothing for Jack to administer between commissions. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-0a5fd39e><h3 data-v-0a5fd39e>Cal.com</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-0a5fd39e>Scheduling</span><p data-v-0a5fd39e> Consultation booking that writes straight to Jack&#39;s calendar, removing the scheduling email thread entirely. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-0a5fd39e><h3 data-v-0a5fd39e>Cloudflare</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-0a5fd39e>Hosting</span><p data-v-0a5fd39e> Edge-delivered on a lightweight build, which keeps the monthly care fee small. The studio&#39;s other running costs are the domain and Stripe&#39;s transaction fee. </p></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="detail-container" data-v-0a5fd39e><h2 data-v-0a5fd39e>What the Client Said</h2><div class="testimonial-card" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="testimonial-quote-mark" data-v-0a5fd39e>&quot;</div><blockquote class="testimonial-text" data-v-0a5fd39e> Quan is phenomenal to work with; he designed a website for my calligraphy business and worked with me for two full months to make sure it was exactly how I hoped it&#39;d be. Everything from personal preferences (i.e. not using AI, but taking actual photos of the work) to pricing structure was convenient and clearly laid out in both our consultations and contract. Quan went above and beyond expectations and would not accept any bonus/tip for his patience and effort. </blockquote><div class="testimonial-author" data-v-0a5fd39e><img${ssrRenderAttr("src", _imports_2)} alt="Jack Passananti" class="testimonial-avatar" loading="lazy" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="testimonial-meta" data-v-0a5fd39e><p class="testimonial-name" data-v-0a5fd39e>Jack Passananti</p><p class="testimonial-role" data-v-0a5fd39e>Writer · Calligrapher · Illuminator, Broad Strokes Studio</p><p class="testimonial-source" data-v-0a5fd39e>Shared on LinkedIn, 4 August 2026</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="detail-container" data-v-0a5fd39e><h2 data-v-0a5fd39e>My Role</h2><p class="section-intro" data-v-0a5fd39e> Two months, end to end, from the first consultation to the first sale: </p><div class="role-list" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="role-item" data-v-0a5fd39e>Ran consultations to understand the craft, the buyer, and what Jack would and would not compromise on.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-0a5fd39e>Worked out the pricing structure with him and laid it out clearly in both the site and the contract.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-0a5fd39e>Designed the visual identity and page architecture around real photographs of real work.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-0a5fd39e>Developed and deployed the full seven-page site.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-0a5fd39e>Set up Stripe payment links per size and framing option, with client reference tagging.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-0a5fd39e>Integrated Cal.com consultation booking into the commission funnel.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-0a5fd39e>Iterated until it matched what Jack had in his head, not what was fastest to ship.</div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="detail-container" data-v-0a5fd39e><h2 data-v-0a5fd39e>Why There Was No Development Fee</h2><blockquote class="featured-quote" data-v-0a5fd39e> Jack tried to pay me a bonus at the end and I turned it down. There was no development fee because that is how we work with every accepted project: a one-person studio putting months into hand-lettered work should be spending its money on paper, gilding, and photography, not on a big upfront bill. Instead, a small monthly fee covers hosting, maintenance and support, and the site earns its keep every time a commission comes in. </blockquote></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="detail-container" data-v-0a5fd39e><h2 data-v-0a5fd39e>Project Status</h2><div class="status-box" data-v-0a5fd39e><span class="status-indicator" data-v-0a5fd39e>Live</span><p data-v-0a5fd39e> The studio is open for commissions and taking payment through the site. Because checkout runs on Stripe payment links and booking runs on Cal.com, Jack can add a size, change a price, or close his calendar without touching code. When the catalogue grows past what payment links handle comfortably, the Astro build is ready to take a proper storefront. Hosting, maintenance and support are covered by the studio&#39;s monthly plan. </p></div></div></section><section class="cta-section" data-v-0a5fd39e><div class="cta-container" data-v-0a5fd39e><h2 data-v-0a5fd39e>Selling Craft That Deserves Better Than a Template?</h2><p data-v-0a5fd39e> We build sites for makers, studios, and independent professionals whose work is the product. Tell us what you make and we will tell you how we would sell it. </p><div class="cta-buttons" data-v-0a5fd39e>`);
