      _push(`<div class="status-badge" data-v-124e8951><span data-v-124e8951>Past Contribution</span></div><img${ssrRenderAttr("src", _imports_0)} alt="WM Smile Generation Uganda Logo" class="hero-logo" data-v-124e8951><h1 data-v-124e8951>WM Smile Generation Uganda</h1><p class="tagline" data-v-124e8951>Official Website</p><div class="hero-meta" data-v-124e8951><span class="meta-tag" data-v-124e8951>Role: Website Administrator &amp; Lead Developer</span><span class="meta-tag" data-v-124e8951>Non-Profit Organization Website</span><span class="meta-tag" data-v-124e8951>Site No Longer Online</span></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-124e8951><div class="detail-container" data-v-124e8951><h2 data-v-124e8951>Overview</h2><p data-v-124e8951> When I worked with them, WM Smile Generation Uganda Limited was a non-profit dedicated to transforming the lives of children and youth across Uganda through quality education, environmental conservation, and refugee child protection. I led the full design and development of their first website, built to communicate their impact, attract donors, and connect the organization with global partners. That site is no longer online, so this page is a record of the work. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-124e8951><div class="detail-container" data-v-124e8951><h2 data-v-124e8951>The Challenge</h2><p data-v-124e8951> The organization had a powerful story but no digital home. Joseph Bumpenje, a Ugandan educator who grew up in extreme hardship, founded WM Smile Generation to ensure no child faces the same barriers he did. The team, spread across Uganda, South Africa, Italy, Nigeria, and Vietnam, needed a professional, trustworthy online presence that could serve multiple goals at once: tell the founder&#39;s story, showcase the mission&#39;s three core pillars, enable donations, and attract partnership opportunities from an international audience. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-124e8951><div class="detail-container" data-v-124e8951><h2 data-v-124e8951>Timeline</h2><div class="highlight-box" data-v-124e8951><span class="highlight-number" data-v-124e8951>3 days</span><span class="highlight-label" data-v-124e8951>from kickoff to launch</span></div><p data-v-124e8951> The organization needed a professional web presence quickly to support ongoing partnership conversations and fundraising efforts. By leveraging Astro&#39;s streamlined development workflow and keeping the scope focused on what mattered most, namely clear storytelling, strong calls-to-action, and a trustworthy design, I was able to go from first commit to live site in a single long weekend. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-124e8951><div class="detail-container" data-v-124e8951><h2 data-v-124e8951>What I Built</h2><p class="section-intro" data-v-124e8951> A clean, purpose-driven website that put the mission front and center and made it easy for visitors to take action. </p><div class="features-grid" data-v-124e8951><div class="feature-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="feature-icon" data-v-124e8951>🏠</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>Landing Page</h3><p data-v-124e8951> Clear value proposition, mission pillars (Education, Nature Awareness, Refugee Support), and prominent calls-to-action for donations and partnerships. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="feature-icon" data-v-124e8951>📖</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>About Page</h3><p data-v-124e8951> The founder&#39;s personal story, organizational vision and mission, guiding principles, and a full team section with bios and photos for all seven team members. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="feature-icon" data-v-124e8951>🎯</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>Our Mission Page</h3><p data-v-124e8951> Deeper context on each of the three focus areas: education, nature awareness, and refugee support. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="feature-icon" data-v-124e8951>🤝</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>Partnership Page</h3><p data-v-124e8951> Designed to attract and onboard organizational partners with clear pathways to collaboration. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="feature-icon" data-v-124e8951>🏅</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>Our Partners Page</h3><p data-v-124e8951> Showcasing existing partnerships to build credibility and trust with potential supporters. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="feature-icon" data-v-124e8951>❤️</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>Donation Page</h3><p data-v-124e8951> A clear, accessible path for supporters to contribute directly to the mission. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="feature-icon" data-v-124e8951>✉️</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>Contact Page</h3><p data-v-124e8951> For general inquiries and engagement from around the world. </p></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-124e8951><div class="detail-container" data-v-124e8951><h2 data-v-124e8951>Design Priorities</h2><div class="priorities-list" data-v-124e8951><div class="priority-item" data-v-124e8951><div class="priority-icon" data-v-124e8951>🎨</div><div class="priority-content" data-v-124e8951><h3 data-v-124e8951>Professional Visual Identity</h3><p data-v-124e8951>Appropriate for an NGO seeking international donors and partners.</p></div></div><div class="priority-item" data-v-124e8951><div class="priority-icon" data-v-124e8951>📱</div><div class="priority-content" data-v-124e8951><h3 data-v-124e8951>Mobile-Responsive Layout</h3><p data-v-124e8951>Accommodating visitors from regions with mobile-first internet usage.</p></div></div><div class="priority-item" data-v-124e8951><div class="priority-icon" data-v-124e8951>📏</div><div class="priority-content" data-v-124e8951><h3 data-v-124e8951>Clear Information Hierarchy</h3><p data-v-124e8951>Within seconds, visitors could see who the organization was, what it did, and how to help.</p></div></div><div class="priority-item" data-v-124e8951><div class="priority-icon" data-v-124e8951>❤️</div><div class="priority-content" data-v-124e8951><h3 data-v-124e8951>Human-Centered Storytelling</h3><p data-v-124e8951>Warm imagery and storytelling that reflected the reality on the ground.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-124e8951><div class="detail-container" data-v-124e8951><h2 data-v-124e8951>Tech Stack &amp; Hosting</h2><div class="tech-grid" data-v-124e8951><div class="tech-card" data-v-124e8951><h3 data-v-124e8951>Astro</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-124e8951>Framework</span><p data-v-124e8951> Chosen for its fast static site generation, minimal JavaScript overhead, and excellent performance on low-bandwidth connections, which mattered for an audience that included visitors from East Africa. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-124e8951><h3 data-v-124e8951>Vercel</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-124e8951>Hosting (Free Tier)</span><p data-v-124e8951> Kept hosting costs at zero for a non-profit that needed every dollar to go to its mission. </p></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-124e8951><div class="detail-container" data-v-124e8951><h2 data-v-124e8951>My Role</h2><p class="section-intro" data-v-124e8951> As Website Administrator, I owned the project end-to-end: </p><div class="role-list" data-v-124e8951><div class="role-item" data-v-124e8951>Gathered requirements from the founder and Director of Operations.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-124e8951>Designed the site architecture and page structure.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-124e8951>Developed and deployed the full website.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-124e8951>Coordinated with the content team (Kayla Pillay, Davide Celentano) to integrate copy and media.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-124e8951>Maintained and updated the site while I was part of the team.</div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-124e8951><div class="detail-container" data-v-124e8951><h2 data-v-124e8951>Where It Stands Now</h2><div class="status-box" data-v-124e8951><span class="status-indicator" data-v-124e8951>No Longer Online</span><p data-v-124e8951> I used to look after this site as the team&#39;s Website Administrator. It has since gone offline, so there is nothing live to link to. Static pages on free hosting kept it light and cost the organization nothing to host while it ran. What the organization does online now is theirs to speak to rather than mine to claim. </p></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-124e8951><div class="detail-container" data-v-124e8951><h2 data-v-124e8951>Why This Project Matters to Me</h2><blockquote class="featured-quote" data-v-124e8951> This is not just a portfolio piece. It&#39;s personal. I believe deeply that technology should serve people who need it most, not just those who can pay for it. WM Smile Generation&#39;s mission, giving vulnerable children access to education and a healthier environment, aligned directly with why I founded Skill-Wanderer. Working alongside this international team of volunteers reinforced something I carry into everything I build: the best technology is the kind that amplifies human compassion. </blockquote></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-124e8951><div class="detail-container" data-v-124e8951><h2 data-v-124e8951>The Team I Worked With</h2><p class="section-intro" data-v-124e8951>Roles as they were while I was part of the team.</p><div class="team-grid" data-v-124e8951><div class="team-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="team-role-icon" data-v-124e8951>👤</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>Joseph Bumpenje</h3><span class="team-role" data-v-124e8951>CEO &amp; Founder</span><span class="team-location" data-v-124e8951>Kampala, Uganda</span></div><div class="team-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="team-role-icon" data-v-124e8951>👤</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>Ornella Gigante</h3><span class="team-role" data-v-124e8951>Director of Operations / Founder of MindyCore</span></div><div class="team-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="team-role-icon" data-v-124e8951>👤</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>Quan Nguyen</h3><span class="team-role" data-v-124e8951>Website Administrator / Founder of Skill-Wanderer</span></div><div class="team-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="team-role-icon" data-v-124e8951>👤</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>Kayla Pillay</h3><span class="team-role" data-v-124e8951>Content Specialist</span><span class="team-location" data-v-124e8951>South Africa</span></div><div class="team-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="team-role-icon" data-v-124e8951>👤</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>Precious Pabalelo Matlala</h3><span class="team-role" data-v-124e8951>Donations &amp; Fundraising Lead</span><span class="team-location" data-v-124e8951>South Africa</span></div><div class="team-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="team-role-icon" data-v-124e8951>👤</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>Muhammad Hanif Danladi</h3><span class="team-role" data-v-124e8951>Coach &amp; Content Creator</span><span class="team-location" data-v-124e8951>Nigeria</span></div><div class="team-card" data-v-124e8951><div class="team-role-icon" data-v-124e8951>👤</div><h3 data-v-124e8951>Davide Celentano</h3><span class="team-role" data-v-124e8951>Agro-Environmental Content Specialist</span><span class="team-location" data-v-124e8951>Italy</span></div></div></div></section><section class="cta-section" data-v-124e8951><div class="cta-container" data-v-124e8951><h2 data-v-124e8951>Have a Mission That Needs a Digital Home?</h2><p data-v-124e8951> We build technology for organizations that make the world better. If you have a non-profit, community project, or social enterprise that needs a web presence, let&#39;s talk. </p><div class="cta-buttons" data-v-124e8951>`);
