      _push(`<div class="status-badge" data-v-e3a8c3b1><span data-v-e3a8c3b1>Live</span></div><img${ssrRenderAttr("src", _imports_0)} alt="The Meek Method" class="hero-logo" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h1 data-v-e3a8c3b1>The Meek Method</h1><p class="tagline" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Decision Coaching Practice, Aimee Meek</p><div class="hero-meta" data-v-e3a8c3b1><span class="meta-tag" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Role: Designer, Developer &amp; Positioning Adviser</span><span class="meta-tag" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Coaching Practice &amp; Newsletter</span><a href="https://themeekmethodcoaching.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="meta-tag link-tag" data-v-e3a8c3b1>themeekmethodcoaching.com →</a></div><div class="fee-banner" data-v-e3a8c3b1><span class="fee-banner-label" data-v-e3a8c3b1>No Development Fee</span><p data-v-e3a8c3b1>Designed, built, and launched with no development fee. The practice is on our monthly hosting, maintenance and support plan.</p></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="detail-container" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h2 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Overview</h2><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> Aimee Meek is an ICF-trained coach and NLP practitioner who spent twelve years as a Special Operations spouse, then went through divorce, sobriety, single parenthood, a career change, and several relocations. Out of that she built a practice around something most coaching ignores: not making the decision, but living with it once the pressure starts. We built the site that makes that distinction legible in about ten seconds, and turns it into three ways to work with her. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="detail-container" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h2 data-v-e3a8c3b1>The Challenge</h2><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> The coaching market is saturated with people promising clarity. Aimee&#39;s offer is the opposite and much harder to explain: you already made the right call, and the discomfort you feel is not evidence that you did not. That is a sharp, unusual position, and a generic coaching site would have flattened it into the same soft language everyone else uses. The build had to protect the specificity, because the specificity is what makes someone recognise themselves and book. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="detail-container" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h2 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Naming the Thing Nobody Names</h2><div class="highlight-box" data-v-e3a8c3b1><span class="highlight-number" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Movement</span><span class="highlight-label" data-v-e3a8c3b1>without collapse, the part after the choice</span></div><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> The whole site turns on one line from Aimee: discomfort can be real without proving the decision was wrong. Everything else, the framework page, the service tiers, the newsletter called The Decision You Keep Circling, is an expansion of that sentence. Getting the positioning right was most of the work. The build followed from it. </p></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="detail-container" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h2 data-v-e3a8c3b1>What I Built</h2><p class="section-intro" data-v-e3a8c3b1> A practice site with a tiered entry path, from a free group session to private coaching. </p><div class="features-grid" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="feature-card" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="feature-icon" data-v-e3a8c3b1>🪨</div><h3 data-v-e3a8c3b1>The Meek Method Page</h3><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> The framework explained on its own terms: judgment stays central, pressure is separated from facts, practical next steps emerge, and support continues afterwards. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="feature-icon" data-v-e3a8c3b1>⏱️</div><h3 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Decision Stabilization Intensive</h3><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> The flagship offer, a 90-minute private session on one decision, with its own dedicated page so it can be linked and sold directly. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="feature-icon" data-v-e3a8c3b1>🧪</div><h3 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Decision Pressure Lab</h3><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> A free monthly small-group session that works as the top of the funnel, letting people experience the method before paying for it. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="feature-icon" data-v-e3a8c3b1>🤝</div><h3 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Private Coaching</h3><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> The ongoing tier, for recurring patterns that show up across decisions rather than in a single one. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="feature-icon" data-v-e3a8c3b1>📬</div><h3 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Newsletter Capture</h3><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> The Decision You Keep Circling, with a cover and a dedicated signup page, so visitors who are not ready to book still enter the practice. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="feature-icon" data-v-e3a8c3b1>📖</div><h3 data-v-e3a8c3b1>About Page</h3><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> Lived experience and professional training side by side, because in this market credibility comes from both and neither alone. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="feature-icon" data-v-e3a8c3b1>✉️</div><h3 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Contact Page</h3><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> A direct enquiry route for people whose situation does not fit neatly into one of the three offers. </p></div><div class="feature-card" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="feature-icon" data-v-e3a8c3b1>♿</div><h3 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Policy Pages</h3><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> Accessibility statement, privacy, cookies, and terms, appropriate for a practice handling sensitive personal context. </p></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="detail-container" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h2 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Tech Stack &amp; Hosting</h2><div class="tech-grid" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="tech-card" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h3 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Astro</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Framework</span><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> Static generation with a self-hosted variable font and preloaded assets, so the site feels calm and instant, which matters for a practice whose whole promise is steadiness. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h3 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Cloudflare</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Hosting</span><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> Edge-delivered on a lightweight build, which keeps the monthly care fee small for a practice that is just starting. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h3 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Web3Forms</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Enquiry &amp; Signup</span><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> Contact and newsletter submissions delivered without a backend, a database, or a monthly form subscription. </p></div><div class="tech-card" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h3 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Structured SEO &amp; llms.txt</h3><span class="tech-label" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Discoverability</span><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> Canonical URLs, Open Graph cards, author markup, and an llms.txt file, so the practice is legible to search engines and to the AI assistants people increasingly ask for recommendations. </p></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="detail-container" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h2 data-v-e3a8c3b1>What the Client Said</h2><div class="testimonial-card" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="testimonial-quote-mark" data-v-e3a8c3b1>&quot;</div><blockquote class="testimonial-text" data-v-e3a8c3b1> Working with Quan Nguyen at Skill-Wanderer has been such a positive experience, and I genuinely cannot recommend him enough. <br data-v-e3a8c3b1><br data-v-e3a8c3b1> When I first started working with Quan on my website for The Meek Method, I had a very clear vision of what I wanted my business to represent, but very little understanding of the technology required to bring it all together. <br data-v-e3a8c3b1><br data-v-e3a8c3b1> Quan has been incredibly patient with me throughout the entire process. He takes the time to explain things, answer my questions, and make sure I understand what we&#39;re doing without ever making me feel rushed or overwhelmed. <br data-v-e3a8c3b1><br data-v-e3a8c3b1> What I appreciate most is that he genuinely cares about the work he does and the people he works with. He pays attention to the smallest details, welcomes feedback, and often catches things or suggests improvements I wouldn&#39;t have known to ask about. <br data-v-e3a8c3b1><br data-v-e3a8c3b1> He didn&#39;t simply build a website and walk away. He has continued to help me with adjustments, technical questions, and the many moving pieces that come with building an online presence for a growing business. <br data-v-e3a8c3b1><br data-v-e3a8c3b1> I&#39;ve also come to really respect the mission behind Skill-Wanderer and Quan&#39;s commitment to using his business to support free education. <br data-v-e3a8c3b1><br data-v-e3a8c3b1> If you&#39;re looking for someone who is knowledgeable, reliable, thoughtful, and genuinely invested in helping your business succeed, I would highly recommend working with Quan. <br data-v-e3a8c3b1><br data-v-e3a8c3b1> I&#39;m incredibly grateful to have him as part of the team helping me build The Meek Method. </blockquote><div class="testimonial-author" data-v-e3a8c3b1><img${ssrRenderAttr("src", _imports_1)} alt="Aimee Meek" class="testimonial-avatar" loading="lazy" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="testimonial-meta" data-v-e3a8c3b1><p class="testimonial-name" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Aimee Meek</p><p class="testimonial-role" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Decision Coach · Creator of The Meek Method</p><p class="testimonial-source" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Shared on LinkedIn</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="detail-container" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h2 data-v-e3a8c3b1>My Role</h2><p class="section-intro" data-v-e3a8c3b1> Positioning first, then the build: </p><div class="role-list" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="role-item" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Worked with Aimee to sharpen a hard-to-explain method into language a stranger recognises immediately.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Structured the offer ladder, from the free Decision Pressure Lab up to private coaching.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Designed the visual identity and a page architecture that stays calm rather than sales-heavy.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Developed and deployed the full site, including the twelve pages and the newsletter funnel.</div><div class="role-item" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Set up enquiry handling, SEO, accessibility, and the policy pages a coaching practice needs.</div></div></div></section><section class="detail-section" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="detail-container" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h2 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Why There Was No Development Fee</h2><blockquote class="featured-quote" data-v-e3a8c3b1> A practice like this is one person betting on an idea before anyone has paid them for it. Charging a development fee at that moment takes money out of exactly the phase where it has the most work to do. So, as with every accepted project, there was no development fee: a small monthly fee covers hosting, maintenance and support instead. The site was live before the first client was. </blockquote></div></section><section class="detail-section darker" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="detail-container" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h2 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Project Status</h2><div class="status-box" data-v-e3a8c3b1><span class="status-indicator" data-v-e3a8c3b1>Live</span><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> The site is live and taking enquiries and newsletter signups, with hosting, maintenance and support covered by the monthly plan. Static generation keeps that running cost small. When the practice is ready for paid scheduling or a client portal, the architecture takes it without a rebuild. </p></div></div></section><section class="cta-section" data-v-e3a8c3b1><div class="cta-container" data-v-e3a8c3b1><h2 data-v-e3a8c3b1>Starting Something and Need It to Land Properly?</h2><p data-v-e3a8c3b1> We help independent professionals find the sentence their whole business rests on, and then build the site that carries it. Tell us what you are starting. </p><div class="cta-buttons" data-v-e3a8c3b1>`);
